UserObject><mxCell id="c184" value="Notes" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#222222;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20.0" y="916.0" width="200.0" height="16.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c185" value="• The Council vote approving the EP position (Art. 294(4) TFEU) took place after the I/A item note of 27 Sep 2024 and before the signature on 23 Oct 2024; its exact date is not in the sources used." style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;fontColor=#444444;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20.0" y="932.0" width="1760.0" height="16.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c186" value="• Trilogues and the Coreper letter are informal steps, not part of Art. 294 TFEU; they follow the Joint Declaration on practical arrangements for the codecision procedure (OJ C 145, 30.6.2007, p. 5), points 7–14." style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;fontColor=#444444;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20.0" y="948.0" width="1760.0" height="16.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c187" value="Labels are shortened; the procedure page lists every event in full with its document and source. Sources: EP Open Data API (procedure events), Cellar procedure file, Council register documents and agendas, EUR-Lex. Our own compilation, not an official record." style="text;html=1;fontSize=9;fontColor=#6f757b;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20.0" y="966.0" width="1760.0" height="16.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c188" value="Steffen Zimmermann · git-z0man.github.io/eu-regulation-timeline · CC BY 4.0" style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#5b646b;align=right;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20.0" y="992.0" width="1760.0" height="16.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>
